   "source": [
    "# Bengaluru Survey Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook documents the data quality checks, cleaning, validation, summary analysis, and visualizations for the Bengaluru ward-level survey dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "efb4525c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load Dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fca5f3c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = Path(\"../data/Bengaluru_Survey_Public_Ward_Analysis.xlsx\")\n",
    "df = pd.read_excel(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Dataset shape:\", df.shape)\n",
    "print(\"\\nColumns:\")\n",
    "print(df.columns.tolist())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d23740e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data Quality Check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8bc15310",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Missing values:\")\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ee37239e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Data Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "The source data has one missing `Commercial` value for Ward 161 (Hosakerehalli). The existing analysis logic records this value as 1239."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cd54912e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "clean_df = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "clean_df.loc[\n",
    "    (clean_df[\"Ward Number\"] == 161) &\n",
    "    (clean_df[\"Ward Name\"] == \"Hosakerehalli\"),\n",
    "    \"Commercial\"\n",
    "] = 1239\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Commercial value for Ward 161:\",\n",
    "      clean_df.loc[clean_df[\"Ward Number\"] == 161, \"Commercial\"].iloc[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6592fe0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Validate Balance Left"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2e517212",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "clean_df[\"Calculated Balance\"] = (\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Total Building Count\"] -\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Verification Done\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "balance_errors = clean_df[\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Balance Left\"] != clean_df[\"Calculated Balance\"]\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Balance validation errors:\", len(balance_errors))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6ee01de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Validate Verification Percentage"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3095cac1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "clean_df[\"Calculated % Done\"] = (\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Verification Done\"] /\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Total Building Count\"] * 100\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "percentage_errors = clean_df[\n",
    "    abs(clean_df[\"% Done\"] - clean_df[\"Calculated % Done\"]) > 0.01\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Percentage validation errors:\", len(percentage_errors))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16d3d329",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Overall Verification Performance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fe06b4dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "overall_verification = (\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Verification Done\"].sum() /\n",
    "    clean_df[\"Total Building Count\"].sum() * 100\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Overall verification percentage:\",\n",
    "      round(overall_verification, 2), \"%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7bffd94",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Ward Count by Corporation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d1c5f4a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ward_count = clean_df.groupby(\"Corporation\")[\"Ward Number\"].count()\n",
    "print(ward_count)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b67fa94",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Recorded Positive Balance by Division"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3a5a29f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "division_backlog = (\n",
    "    clean_df.groupby(\"Division\")[\"Balance Left\"]\n",
    "    .sum()\n",
    "    .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "positive_backlog = division_backlog[division_backlog > 0]\n",
    "print(positive_backlog)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bc6c436d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Top Wards by Recorded Positive Balance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4283e07d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "top_backlog_wards = (\n",
    "    clean_df[clean_df[\"Balance Left\"] > 0]\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"Balance Left\", ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(top_backlog_wards[\n",
    "    [\"Ward Number\", \"Ward Name\", \"Division\", \"Balance Left\"]\n",
    "].head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "614725cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Property Type Totals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "10106be9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "property_totals = clean_df[\n",
    "    [\"Residential Households\", \"Commercial\", \"Apartments\"]\n",
    "].sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(property_totals)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bd9a0d39",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Visualizations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8f1b88b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Top 10 wards\n",
    "top = clean_df[clean_df[\"Balance Left\"] > 0].sort_values(\n",
    "    \"Balance Left\", ascending=False\n",
    ").head(10).sort_values(\"Balance Left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n",
    "plt.barh(top[\"Ward Name\"], top[\"Balance Left\"])\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Recorded Balance Left\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Ward\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Top 10 Wards by Recorded Positive Balance\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Property totals\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\n",
    "pt = clean_df[\n",
    "    [\"Residential Households\", \"Commercial\", \"Apartments\"]\n",
    "].sum()\n",
    "plt.bar(pt.index, pt.values)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Property Type Totals\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=15)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b9c486df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Final Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Temporary validation columns are removed before the final analysis dataframe is retained."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f0b548e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "clean_df = clean_df.drop(\n",
    "    columns=[\"Calculated Balance\", \"Calculated % Done\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Final cleaned dataset shape:\", clean_df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2766996",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "- The dataset contains 198 ward records and 11 source columns.\n",
    "- Balance and verification-percentage calculations validate against the source values within the checks used above.\n",
    "- The overall verification percentage is calculated from total verification done divided by total building count.\n",
    "- Ward-level and division-level recorded positive balances are summarized to identify where remaining recorded balance is concentrated.\n",
    "- Property totals are calculated after applying the documented Ward 161 Commercial correction."
   ]
  }
